      "content": "It's incredibly painful to feel like you're running in circles while others seem to glide through life. But being \"fundamentally flawed\" is a story your exhaustion is telling you—not the truth about who you are. Struggling doesn't mean you're meant to suffer forever; it means you're human, and your pain is valid, not a verdict. And no, I don't think anyone is born broken—just some of us carry heavier storms, and that doesn't make you less worthy of peace. You don't have to pretend everything's fine, but please don't give up on the possibility that things can feel different.",
